@startuml
title P1 Transmission Protocol and Scheduler Components
left to right direction
skinparam componentStyle rectangle

actor "Pulsar app\ncontrol actor" as App
actor "Telegram adapter" as Tg
component "History and presence\nsurfaces" as History

rectangle "Coordinator" {
  component "Transmission HTTP API\nPOST/GET/cancel" as API
  component "Audience Resolver" as Resolver
  component "Transmission Store\ntransmissions + targets + blocks" as Store
  component "Overlay Controller\nprepare barrier + FIFO + receipts" as Scheduler
  component "Legacy Voice Bridge\nSession FSM after_current" as Legacy
  component "WS Hub\ncapability-aware routing" as Hub
}

database "Media Store\nmedia rows + bytes" as Media
component "Windows node client\nprepare/ready/play/cancel" as Win
component "macOS node client\nprepare/ready/play/cancel" as Mac
component "Legacy node\nplay_voice only" as Old

App --> API : create/status/cancel
Tg --> API : create/status/cancel
API --> Media : validate media\nownership + ready state
API --> Resolver : audience -> targets
API --> Store : accepted transmission\n+ target snapshot

Scheduler --> Store : receipt transitions\n+ cancel state
Scheduler --> Hub : prepare/play/cancel
Scheduler --> Legacy : downgrade to\nafter_current
Hub --> Scheduler : ready/started/\nended/failed + DND

Hub --> Win
Hub --> Mac
Hub --> Old : play_voice

Media --> Win : GET /media/{id}
Media --> Mac : GET /media/{id}
Store --> History : status/receipts/\npresence view

note right of Store
Target snapshots are the only
phase-one media ACL source.
Knowing a media_id alone
must not authorize download.
end note

note bottom of Scheduler
One controller owns overlay + interrupt FIFO for the whole effective
playback domain (orbit when separate, stable approach identity when joined).
Interrupt fallback is never invented by the scheduler.
end note
@enduml
